{"schema":1,
"kind":"trace",
"id":"prefix_min",
"source":"prefix_min.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef fast(values):\n    n = len(values)\n    total = 0\n    prefix = [0]\n    for v in values:\n        total += v\n        prefix.append(total)\n    low = prefix[0]\n    best = values[0]\n    for j in range(n):\n        end = prefix[j + 1]\n        cand = end - low\n        best = max(best, cand)\n        low = min(low, end)\n    return best\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    tokens = raw.split()\n    n = int(tokens[0])\n    nums = tokens[1:n + 1]\n    values = list(map(int, nums))\n    print(fast(values))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The prefix-sum method with a running minimum, run on two or three numbers. The program reads the numbers, builds the prefix array with a running total, then loops over each end j. For each end it subtracts low, the smallest prefix entry so far, to get the best sum ending there, keeps the largest in best, and lowers low whenever a smaller entry appears. It prints best.",
